{
  "document": "23EC35-annex1",
  "page": 3,
  "task": "SOURCE_REGION_MATERIALITY",
  "role": "qualification-first",
  "assessment_basis": "Visual inspection of the supplied rendered page. Classifications concern printed text and extraction fidelity, not legal applicability.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "issue_id": "region.df66e1d4416b7a5edecd0c98",
      "printed_text": "8. Streamlining Threshold",
      "classification": "TEXT_ORDER",
      "assessment": "The printed section number “8.” appears immediately before the underlined heading “Streamlining Threshold”, after paragraph 7.3(b). This insertion and the deletion in region.24ed85bae8291b3529bb54a9 concern the same printed number and together indicate a relocation in extraction order, rather than a purely typographic difference.",
      "uncertainty": "The supplied token intervals do not show enough surrounding extracted text to determine which extraction places the number correctly."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.24ed85bae8291b3529bb54a9",
      "printed_text": "8. Streamlining Threshold",
      "classification": "TEXT_ORDER",
      "assessment": "The printed “8.” is present and labels “Streamlining Threshold”. Read together with region.df66e1d4416b7a5edecd0c98, the deletion indicates relocation of this heading number, not an established net omission from the extraction.",
      "uncertainty": "Correct placement in either complete extraction cannot be established from these isolated intervals."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.71c24d5e12e2bab653c8e6dc",
      "printed_text": [
        {
          "text": "5. Investment objectives",
          "position": "Top of the page's main text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Page 3 of 7",
          "position": "Bottom-right footer"
        }
      ],
      "classification": "TEXT_OMISSION_AND_LAYOUT_ORDER",
      "assessment": "Both “5.” and “Page 3 of 7” are visibly printed. Their removal omits a section number and pagination text; it is not typographic normalization. The left token sequence places the footer before the top section number, which does not reflect the printed spatial arrangement. The numerous other locations matching “of” or “7” are not evidence that those body-text occurrences were deleted by this issue.",
      "uncertainty": "The supplied change establishes deletion from this interval, but does not establish whether either item is retained elsewhere in the complete right extraction."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.1316d13555f4c8e7edfbf364",
      "printed_text": "5.1 Intermediaries should not apply the Streamlined Approach when dealing with conservative clients",
      "classification": "TEXT_OMISSION",
      "assessment": "“5.1” is a clearly printed paragraph number. Deleting it omits structural text rather than changing typography.",
      "uncertainty": "None concerning the printed paragraph number."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.bc405057047515f7201d9095",
      "printed_text": "6. Intermediaries should only execute investment transactions for an SPI under the Streamlined Approach",
      "classification": "TEXT_OMISSION",
      "assessment": "“6.” is visibly printed beside the paragraph beneath “(B) Eligible investment transactions”. Its deletion omits the paragraph number.",
      "uncertainty": "None concerning the printed paragraph number."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.a88155a6f653c12219eaa9ea",
      "printed_text": "(“Eligible Investment Transactions”).",
      "classification": "TYPOGRAPHIC",
      "assessment": "The printed opening quotation mark is a curly double quotation mark. The right extraction replaces it with a straight single quotation mark. The opening parenthesis and the word “Eligible” remain; the difference concerns quotation-mark typography.",
      "uncertainty": "None material to this transcription."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.018a552597ba9ee313376e7f",
      "printed_text": [
        "(“Eligible Investment Transactions”).",
        "7. Product Category"
      ],
      "classification": "MIXED_TYPOGRAPHIC_AND_TEXT_OMISSION",
      "assessment": "The source closes the defined phrase with a curly double quotation mark, followed by a closing parenthesis and period. Replacing that quotation mark with a straight single quotation mark is typographic. Separately, the source prints “7.” before the next heading, “Product Category”; deleting that number omits structural text.",
      "uncertainty": "None concerning the printed quotation mark or heading number."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.fb7b474a9b18fc97c56f9fd2",
      "printed_text": "7.1 Intermediaries should devise (or adjust as appropriate) Product Categories",
      "classification": "TEXT_OMISSION",
      "assessment": "The paragraph number “7.1” is visibly printed. Its deletion is an omission of structural text, not a typographic difference.",
      "uncertainty": "None concerning the printed paragraph number."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.f280631ab51437c66f1f6306",
      "printed_text": "7.2 The SPI should specify the Product Categories within which investment transactions could be executed under a Streamlined Approach.",
      "classification": "TEXT_OMISSION",
      "assessment": "The paragraph number “7.2” is visibly printed. Its deletion omits structural text.",
      "uncertainty": "None concerning the printed paragraph number."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.56a09a9f9e0033d73edefa8d",
      "printed_text": "the “Product Category Information Statement”",
      "classification": "TYPOGRAPHIC",
      "assessment": "The source uses a curly opening double quotation mark before “Product”. The right extraction substitutes a straight single quotation mark. The words are unchanged. The defined phrase continues across a printed line break.",
      "uncertainty": "None material to this transcription."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.6912131b88dd98385ec69d25",
      "printed_text": "Information Statement” eg, in the form of an information booklet/ hyperlinks).",
      "classification": "TYPOGRAPHIC",
      "assessment": "The source uses a curly closing double quotation mark immediately after “Statement”. The right extraction substitutes a straight single quotation mark. This changes quotation-mark typography without omitting the word.",
      "uncertainty": "None concerning the affected quotation mark."
    },
    {
      "issue_id": "region.7f8841962c2601bea07ad712",
      "printed_text": [
        {
          "paragraph": "7.2",
          "text": "to facilitate the SPI’s understanding of the"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": "8.1",
          "text": "a percentage relative to the SPI’s assets under management (“AUM”) with the"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": "8.2",
          "text": "including the SPI’s rationale that provides support for setting such threshold."
        }
      ],
      "classification": "TYPOGRAPHIC",
      "assessment": "Each listed location prints “SPI’s” with a curly apostrophe. “SPI's” substitutes a straight apostrophe and preserves the possessive wording.",
      "uncertainty": "The change identifies one token replacement but lists three matching locations. The isolated interval does not establish which occurrence it targets; the typographic assessment is the same at all three."
    }
  ],
  "page_observations": {
    "superscripts_and_footnotes": "No superscript footnote markers or footnote text are visible on this page. “Page 3 of 7” is a footer.",
    "table_headings": "No table is visible. “Investment objectives”, “Product Category”, and “Streamlining Threshold” are underlined section headings; “(B) Eligible investment transactions” is a bold heading.",
    "qualification_structure": "Paragraph 7.3 introduces its conditions with “unless –”. Subparagraph (a) ends with “or”, connecting it to subparagraph (b). These alternatives are visibly separate from the subsequent section 8 heading.",
    "scope_limit": "The assessment does not determine legal applicability or certify either complete extraction as correct."
  }
}
